    "title": "Downtown Staple Leni's Cafe Serving Its Last Plate After 50 Years - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Melissa Davenport ,\n8 hours ago Leni's Cafe, the old-school diner on Baronne Street that has kept downtown New Orleans fed for decades, is calling it quits at the end of May after roughly 50 years in business. Owners Pete and Despina Patselikos say they are retiring and plan to serve their final meal on May 29, closing the book on a neighborhood fixture generations of workers and regulars treated like a second home. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
